# Rare decay: B+ -> K*+ l+ l- (l = e, mu; 50/50), BTOSLLBALL model.
# K*+ -> K+ pi0 or K_S0 pi+, 50/50. That matches the physical ratio (each is
# 1/3 of K*+ decays: K*+ -> K0 pi+ is 2/3 and K0 -> K_S0 is 1/2), but the two
# together are only 2/3 of K*+ decays -- apply that factor at analysis time.
#
# Fix vs. PR #1: the Upsilon(4S) line must produce CHARGED B pairs. The PR
# version decayed Upsilon(4S) -> B0sig anti-B0sig, and since no B0sig decay
# is defined in this file, both B0s fell back to generic decays: the sample
# contained no K*+ l+ l- signal at all.
# One B -> signal, the other generic (same form as official EWP dec files,
# e.g. 1210432000.dec). B+sig/B-sig aliases come from DECAY_BELLE2.DEC.

Alias      K*+sig       K*+
Alias      K*-sig       K*-
ChargeConj K*+sig       K*-sig

Decay Upsilon(4S)
0.500  B+sig B-                      VSS;
0.500  B-sig B+                      VSS;
Enddecay

Decay B+sig
0.500  K*+sig e+  e-                 PHOTOS BTOSLLBALL;
0.500  K*+sig mu+ mu-                PHOTOS BTOSLLBALL;
Enddecay
CDecay B-sig

Decay K*+sig
0.500  K+    pi0                     VSS;
0.500  K_S0  pi+                     VSS;
Enddecay
CDecay K*-sig

End
